---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { ShieldCheck, Lock, Globe, FileText, CheckCircle2 } from 'lucide-react';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Colformly';
const description = 'Official Privacy Policy, Google User Data Disclosures, and Limited Use Compliance for Colformly.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonical="https://colformly.pages.dev/privacy">
  <main class="pt-32 sm:pt-40 pb-24 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    {/* Page Header */}
    <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 dark:border-white/10 pb-8 mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-teal-500/10 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 text-xs font-mono font-medium mb-4">
        <ShieldCheck class="w-4 h-4" />
        <span>Legal &amp; Google Workspace Compliance</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-display font-black text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-3">
        Effective Date: November 21, 2026 • Application Name: Colformly
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Prose Content */}
    <div class="space-y-10 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-body text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
      {/* 1. Introduction */}
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          1. Introduction
        </h2>
        <p>
          Colformly (&quot;we,&quot; &quot;our,&quot; or &quot;the Platform&quot;), operated by EdgeCors Engineering,
          provides institutional exam-as-a-service infrastructure for colleges, universities, academies, and
          coaching institutes. This Privacy Policy details our practices concerning data collection, processing,
          storage, and explicit safeguards regarding Google User Data accessed via OAuth 2.0.
        </p>
      </section>

      {/* 2. Google User Data & Scopes */}
      <section class="space-y-4 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-teal-50/50 dark:bg-teal-950/20 border border-teal-500/30">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-teal-700 dark:text-teal-300">
          <Globe class="w-6 h-6 shrink-0" />
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            2. Google User Data &amp; Scopes Disclosure
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Colformly integrates with Google Workspace APIs to streamline institutional authentication and
          faculty exam orchestration. We request the minimum necessary scopes:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 pt-2">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-[#0D111A] border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-white/10 space-y-1.5">
            <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm">
              A. General Authentication (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400">openid</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400">email</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400">profile</code>)
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Requested for all users (students, faculty, administrators) strictly to authenticate identity, verify
              membership in the institution&apos;s authorized Google Workspace domain (e.g., <code class="font-mono">@campus.edu.in</code>),
              and populate the user&apos;s display name and profile picture.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-[#0D111A] border border-slate-200/80 dark:border-white/10 space-y-1.5">
            <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white text-sm">
              B. Optional Faculty Incremental Scopes (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400">drive.file</code> and <code class="font-mono text-xs text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400">forms.body</code>)
            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
              Requested exclusively from verified faculty members when they choose to sync an assessment to their Google
              Workspace. This permission is strictly utilized to:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 space-y-1 pt-1">
              <li>Create a designated subject folder (e.g., <code class="font-mono">Colformly / Course / Test</code>) in the teacher&apos;s Google Drive.</li>
              <li>Create and update the Google Form representing the test questions.</li>
              <li>Read the linked Google Sheet identifier (<code class="font-mono">linkedSheetId</code>) to verify responses export.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-semibold pt-1">
              Colformly NEVER accesses, reads, modifies, or deletes any files, folders, or spreadsheets in the faculty member&apos;s Google Drive that were not created directly by Colformly.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* 3. Mandatory Google Limited Use Statement */}
      <section class="space-y-4 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl bg-slate-100 dark:bg-white/5 border border-slate-200 dark:border-white/10">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-xl text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <FileText class="w-5 h-5 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400" />
          <span>3. Google API Services User Data Policy Compliance</span>
        </h2>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-[#07090E] border border-slate-300 dark:border-white/15 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white italic leading-relaxed">
          &quot;Colformly&apos;s use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the{' '}
          <a
            href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="underline text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400"
          >
            Google API Services User Data Policy
          </a>
          , including the Limited Use requirements.&quot;
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          In strict compliance with these requirements:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <CheckCircle2 class="w-4 h-4 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 shrink-0" />
            <span>Google user data is NEVER sold, leased, or traded to third parties or data brokers.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <CheckCircle2 class="w-4 h-4 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 shrink-0" />
            <span>Google user data is NEVER used for targeted advertising or user surveillance.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <CheckCircle2 class="w-4 h-4 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 shrink-0" />
            <span>Google user data is NEVER used to train generalized artificial intelligence or machine learning models.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* 4. Token Encryption & Security */}
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <Lock class="w-5 h-5 text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400" />
          <span>4. Token Storage &amp; Encryption Standards</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          Faculty OAuth refresh tokens are encrypted at rest using Web Crypto standard{' '}
          <strong class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white">AES-256-GCM</strong> encryption with 12-byte random initialization
          vectors (IVs). Tokens are never stored in plain text, never exposed to client browsers, and reside in a database table
          protected by PostgreSQL Row-Level Security (RLS) accessible exclusively by our backend Cloudflare Workers via
          dedicated service-role credentials.
        </p>
      </section>

      {/* 5. Sub-processors */}
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          5. Third-Party Sub-Processors
        </h2>
        <p>
          We partner exclusively with verified cloud providers to deliver high-availability edge execution:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          <li><strong>Supabase (AWS ap-south-1):</strong> Database persistence &amp; institutional tenant isolation.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> Edge Workers routing, SSL/TLS termination, and instant paper grading.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Workspace APIs:</strong> Authentication, Google Drive folder creation, and Google Forms sync.</li>
          <li><strong>Groq &amp; Google Gemini APIs:</strong> Question generation (strictly processing teacher prompt text; zero Google OAuth tokens or student answers are shared).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      {/* 6. User Rights, Revocation & Deletion */}
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
          6. User Rights &amp; Google Access Revocation
        </h2>
        <p>
          You retain full authority over your connected Google account and academic records:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          <li>
            <strong>Instant Revocation:</strong> You can revoke Colformly&apos;s access at any time via your{' '}
            <a
              href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="underline text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 font-semibold"
            >
              Google Account Third-Party Access Manager
            </a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Data Deletion Requests:</strong> Institutions and faculty may request full removal of account records,
            tokens, and assessment logs by emailing{' '}
            <a href="mailto:support@edgecors.com" class="underline text-teal-600 dark:text-teal-400 font-mono font-bold">
              support@edgecors.com
            </a>
            . All associated data will be permanently wiped within 30 days.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
